  "version": "0.1.0",
  "notes": "The first early access preview of Pyxida: a calm command center in plain files you own, built to work with AI agents. This is a preview: expect bugs and breaking changes before the public launch, and keep a backup of your folder.\n\n### Added\n- Today: tasks for the day, no-day tasks that carry over until done, deadlines shown as chips, nested and foldable subtasks, recurring tasks and reminders.\n- Calendar: your Mac, Google and subscribed calendars plus events in your folder. Monday-first weeks, a month view, one-click Join for Teams, Zoom and Meet, meeting notes from events, events from plain text in English and Greek, and drag tasks onto days.\n- Notes in Markdown with live preview, Vim keys, sketches, and version history with diff and restore.\n- Money with your own categories and budgets, Learning, Projects and Excalidraw sketches.\n- Vault: encrypted passwords and 2FA codes with a separate master password, a generator and imports from Bitwarden, 1Password and Chrome.\n- AI agents: the `pyxida` command line and an MCP server with the same tools, one-click setup for Claude, Copilot, Cursor and VS Code, and changes only when you allow them.\n- Ask Pyxida: an assistant that proposes changes and waits for your approval, with your own AI key.\n- Pyxida Sync (optional): end-to-end encrypted sync, the phone app at pyxida.dev/app that works offline, reminders on your phone and your Mac calendars on the go.\n- Quick capture from the phone share sheet, iOS Shortcuts and pyxida:// links.\n- English and Greek, light and dark themes, a sidebar in your order, and signed in-app updates.\n- Early access keys that work offline after a one-time activation, on up to 3 devices; deactivate a device in Settings to free a seat.\n- Report a bug from the sidebar, the phone top bar or Settings, with an optional diagnostics preview that never includes your notes, tasks or calendar.",
